## Example: Common Mistake & Fix

### Mistake #3 – Capturing Loop Variables

```csharp
public IEnumerable<Func<int>> CreateFuncs()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 3; i++)
        yield return () => i;   // BAD: all lambdas return 3
}
```

> **Result**: Every lambda returns `3`, because it captures the *loop variable* `i`, not its value at each iteration.

#### Fix

```csharp
public IEnumerable<Func<int>> CreateFuncs()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 3; i++)
    {
        int local = i;          // Capture the value, not the variable
        yield return () => local;
    }
}
```

---

### Mistake #6 – Mixing `yield` and `await`

```csharp
public async IEnumerable<string> ReadFilesAsync()
{
    foreach (var file in Directory.GetFiles("."))
    {
        var content = await File.ReadAllTextAsync(file);
        yield return content; // ❌ Cannot use yield with async
    }
}
```

#### Fix

Use an async stream:

```csharp
public async IAsyncEnumerable<string> ReadFilesAsync()
{
    foreach (var file in Directory.GetFiles("."))
    {
        var content = await File.ReadAllTextAsync(file);
        yield return content;
    }
}
```

Now you can consume with `await foreach`.

